# Conviva DPI JS SDK GTM Template

## Overview
Google Tag Manager community template for the Conviva DPI JS SDK. Source lives in `libs/`; `template.tpl` is generated — never edit it by hand.

## Commands
- `pnpm install` — dependencies
- `pnpm build` — `template.tpl` + `src/generated-types.ts` from `libs/`
- `pnpm test` — Jest (100% coverage on `libs/sandboxed-js.js`)
- `pnpm dev` — Vite harness (`index.html` + polyfills)
- `pnpm sync` — split `template.tpl` → `libs/` (after GTM dashboard export)
- `pnpm test:e2e` — Playwright smoke on dev harness

## Do not edit manually
- `template.tpl` (run `pnpm build`)
- `src/generated-types.ts` (run `pnpm build`)
- Prefer editing `libs/template-info.json`, `libs/template-parameters.json`, `libs/sandboxed-js.js`

## sandboxed-js.js
- Single file, no npm imports — only GTM `require('<api>')` APIs
- Test hatch: `// exports:start` … `// exports:end` (stripped from published template)
- SDK CDN version: `SDK_VERSION` / `REPLAY_SDK_VERSION` constants at top
- **No breaking changes** to field names or tag behavior without a major release note

## TypeScript / tests
- Single quotes, 2 spaces, semicolons
- `tests/kitchen-sink.ts` — shared mock `data` for tests and harness
- Unit tests use `tests/helpers/sandbox-test-env.ts` and `__EXPORTS__`
- After schema changes: update kitchen-sink + snapshots

## GTM validation
- Local `pnpm dev` uses polyfills — not a substitute for **tagmanager.google.com Preview**
- `___TESTS___` scenarios in `template.tpl.ejs` run in GTM on Save

## Branching
- Tooling work merges to `develop` first; `main` only after full plan verification
